+# Root cold review of sharper simultaneous estimate
+
+Mathematical disposition PASS for native proof SHA256 230e7f325100b27e2f1f1642383f526fc52be7e23792e42f5981b9f8e6720b31. Root first froze an independent deliberately crude k98/beta estimate and n200 sufficient sequence (rootproof8ab50837...), then read the full native proof. The sharper normalization identity preserves the Gaussian factor and is valid: p-g=(n-n0)/Ztilde+g(Z0-Ztilde)/Ztilde. The two source covariance eigenvalues have multiplicity8, determinant~k^-8, so normalized Gaussian L2 norm~k2; its polynomial weighted norms have the same growth because the squared Gaussian covariance is uniformly bounded above. This reduces the second normalization term from root's coarse k98 to k52. No Gaussian-peak bound uniform in k is assumed.
+
+Root independently checked uniform fixed-chart E_k>=E1 positivity/gap, affine k growth of action derivatives, second epsilon derivative k2 Gaussian domination, exact two-source first coefficient cancellation, determinant degree12 and partition k^-48, beta>=Ck50 denominator threshold, source cutoff volume beta8 and L2-tail beta64 exp(-gap beta), source half-density evenness, and beta^-4 off-chart operator scaling. Fixed polynomial weights on nuisance-complement tails add only beta polynomials absorbed by the exponential; they do not alter the k exponent. The Gaussian density peak can be bounded by Ck4; its source-chart tail is safely absorbed by k52/beta.
+
+The Gaussian ground eigenvalue stays between fixed positive constants, so actual norm stabilization requires beta>=Ck52 and preserves the uniform bound. The oscillator coordinate map is unitary and adds no k loss. With k_n=4n2/(5t2), beta_n=n108, n*k_n52/beta_n=O_t(n^-3). The clock parameter difference n*t_k-t=O_t(n^-2) gives norm convergence to exp(-tN) by the spectral supremum bound. Actual n-th powers versus repeated chart compression are controlled by a separate contractive telescope.
+
+The source-compression composition contract remains explicit and load-bearing: powers of I*TI generally differ from I*T^nI. The result supplies a simultaneous sequence of repeated reduced operators, not a microscopic full-slab or physical-time law. The huge sufficient exponent108 and unspecified constants/onset do not offer finite-resource accuracy. No audit verdict or framework closure follows. Independent primary review of root's base bounds and native sharper identity is still being collected before canonical publication.
